Looks like Mysql and Postgres are supported ( #2983 )
Meanwhile, here is generic workaround I use for **sqlite** (ActiveRecord pattern):
```ts
function insertOrIgnore<
  Model extends typeof BaseEntity,
  Instance = InstanceType<Model>
>(
  model: Model,
  values: Array<{ [key in keyof Instance]: Instance[key] }>,
) {
  const q = model
    .createQueryBuilder()
    .insert()
    .into(model)
    .values(values)

  const [sql, args] = q.getQueryAndParameters()
  const nsql = sql.replace('INSERT INTO', 'INSERT OR IGNORE INTO')

  return getConnection().manager.query(nsql, args)
}
```
